    {
      "id": "07",
      "title": "Break one line and recover",
      "text": "This time I have left out the closing parenthesis. Depending on how you entered the line, the interactive shell may wait for more input, or Python may report a syntax error when the incomplete statement is submitted. In a saved file, the missing parenthesis prevents the file from running normally.\n\nA syntax error does not mean you cannot program. It means Python could not read the instruction in its current form. Compare the opening and closing punctuation, add the missing parenthesis, and run the corrected line. Change one thing, then check again.",
