    {
      "id": "09",
      "title": "Resolve the opening puzzle",
      "text": "Here is why our first two examples looked different. In the interactive shell, Python normally displays the result of an expression for you. In a saved script, writing an expression by itself does not ask Python to display it. The calculation still happens, but there is no printed output. Use print when your script needs to show the result.\n\nWe have now delivered the opening promise: you can run a saved Python file and explain why it prints something, or why it stays quiet. The shell helps you experiment; the file keeps the instructions you want to repeat.",
